  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts, and it passes typecheck. I couldn't run it or build it with vite, so the frame itself is unchecked.\n\n- **Water mesh:** a 256×256 subdivided grid (320 m wide) with a custom GLSL material. The vertex shader sums 5 directional waves using a peaked sine and computes the normal analytically. The time uniform `waveClock` is updated every frame in `onFrame`.\n- **Fragment shader:**\n  - Fbm value-noise ripples perturb the normal, fading out with distance.\n  - A Schlick fresnel mixes the deep/shallow water colour with the reflected sky.\n  - A sharp-plus-wide sun specular lobe adds the glint.\n  - Distance fog blends the far water into the horizon colour.\n- **Sky:** a `sky.gradient` dome with a sun, using the same zenith, horizon and sun values the water shader uses for its reflection. I guessed how the engine maps its `exponent` onto the gradient, so the reflected sky may not match the dome exactly.\n- **Camera and colour:** the camera sits 2.6 m above the water and looks toward the horizon. Output tone mapping is `none`, and the shader converts its sRGB colours to linear itself, so colours should appear as authored rather than washed out.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set once `app.ready()` resolves and a following animation frame has run.\n\n",
